{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1278542-trolle-tr\u00e4ume-tiefe-w\u00e4lder-got-a-copy-pictures-within","id":1278542,"title":"Trolle, Tr\u00e4ume, Tiefe W\u00e4lder - got a copy! Pictures within!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-04T04:40:52-08:00","id":1278542,"title":"Trolle, Tr\u00e4ume, Tiefe W\u00e4lder - got a copy! Pictures within!","content":"I was absurdly lucky and recently managed to procure a copy of the licensed German sourcebook, Trolle, Tr\u00e4ume, Tiefe W\u00e4lder. <br /> <br /> I don't speak German and haven't yet had time to do any serious work with Google Translate (though I hope to eventually) but I do have a few pictures to share. I apologise for the quality. I only have my phone camera and it's hard to keep all the text in clear focus. I'm hoping this is mostly readable to German speakers at least. <br /> <br /> I also hope this doesn't pose a copyright issue. I'm hoping since this is just a small sample and since it's not available commercially (or really at all any more!) the rights holders won't take offense. <br /> <br /> Anyway, below are images of the front cover and index page, the two pages covering the Wolpertinger and Wichtel (as I believewas previously reported here neither seem to have proper birthrights or frailties), and one of the appendixes which I think has a grid showing compatible and uncompatible seelie/unseelie legacies? I haven't seen anything like that in any other Changeling book so I thought others might find this interesting too. <br /> <br /> <b>The forum doesn't recognise the pictures as valid attachments so here are download links. If anyone else can get them to embed properly, please feel free!</b><br /> <br /> Cover:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.mediafire.com/file/468t4817lvabfa9/20181228_181922.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.mediafire.com/file/468t4...228_181922.jpg</a><br /> <br /> Index:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.mediafire.com/file/t8b16o9a35nglfq/20181228_181938.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.mediafire.com/file/t8b16...228_181938.jpg</a><br /> <br /> Wolpertinger:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.mediafire.com/file/kx3d6gaoau8qkbp/20181228_182032.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.mediafire.com/file/kx3d6...228_182032.jpg</a><br /> <br /> Wichtel:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.mediafire.com/file/bfi71m80wypfz27/20181228_182035.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.mediafire.com/file/bfi71...228_182035.jpg</a><br /> <br /> Appendix Info 1:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.mediafire.com/file/aqx37er81r0r1hm/20181228_182059.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.mediafire.com/file/aqx37...228_182059.jpg</a><br /> <br /> Appendix Info 2:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.mediafire.com/file/jmn2q3tdsl4loxo/20181228_182112.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.mediafire.com/file/jmn2q...228_182112.jpg</a><br /> <br /> Happy to answer any further questions, or receive any suggestions on how to further share this content, but again, I don't speak German... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":".  attachment shenanigans 01-04-2019, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T06:07:55-08:00","id":1279176,"title":"","content":"The Wolpertinger and Wichtel in this book are not full Kiths. There are no Birthrights and Frailties listed here, as they are described as rather being chimera instead of Kithain.<br /> <br /> The grid in appendix one describes the rather complex nature of german Kithain (or rather, specifically those of Th\u00fcringen), who don't go by a seelie/unseelie nature. The book describes them still using a combination of the Legacies but not weighted against another but rather with both sides equaly strong. The table lists how stable these combinations are (the seelie legacys are the ones above, while unseelie legacies are listed on the left). There are a few unstable (&quot;labil&quot;) combinations and a few that are not allowed (&quot;nein&quot;). An unstable combination results in lower starting Willpower and lower starting Banality (one dot less for each) and the character is closer to the first threshold of bedlam.<br /> <br /> Edit: German is my first language and I've tried to get this book for a few years now, but was rather unlucky. The book looks quite interesting, but it seems like it's trying a bit too hard to make german Kithain special in any way (as in: I don't really understand why this change was necessary.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","user":"TheVarulfen","date":". 01-07-2019, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}